// S4 -- "The bank", `Reports/lab-behaviour-scenarios-2026-09-06.md`.
// The environment-side half of the shelter question the 2026-09-05 work
// concluded was all animal: from a flat floor, `(Bias, Dig)` digs a pit open
// to the sky, and a pit is not shelter -- ants were in the open on 66.2% of
// ticks and the non-digger still won. From the foot of a *vertical face* the
// same verb produces a horizontal gallery on the first bite, so the bed's
// job here is to give the ant's existing dig verb the right shape to work
// with rather than to change the verb.
//
// The bank is 16 rows of soil raised over the right 308 columns (`x=200` to
// the shell at `508`), the colony founded at its foot so digging *into* the
// face is the short route home, and beetles placed on top where they can
// walk but a one-wide gallery keeps them out. `exposure_cost_per_cell` is
// turned up from its shipped 0.0 -- shelter cannot be selected for while
// standing outside costs nothing -- to 0.05, the setting the flat null
// (`the_floor.ron`) was measured at.
//
// **Soil is a Powder, so the bed's real shape is a slope, not the vertical
// face it is authored as.** Measured with a rebuilt `labshot scenario=
// the_bank frames=0,3000,24000`, reading the leftmost column (right of the
// stone shell) whose surface still stands above y=160: the wall starts
// exactly at x=200 (the fill's own left edge, width 308) at frame 0, and by
// frame 3000 that leftmost raised column is x=50 -- unchanged at frame
// 24000, so the slump is not still running; it finished inside the first
// eighth of the horizon. **Read that number for what it counts**: a single
// grain that rolled to x=50 moves it as far as a whole ramp would, and the
// contact sheet shows the bulk of the slope inside the last fifty columns
// before x=200, with the bank top untouched at full height. So whoever runs
// S4 meets a short ramp up to the face rather than a cliff: a route to the
// face is partly a walk up a slope before any digging happens.
//
// **Food per 6,000-frame window against the colony's idle burn**: an ant
// idles at 0.10 energy/tick, so 52 ants burn 52 * 0.10 * 6000 = 31,200 per
// window. The 20-cell windfall heap is 19,200 (61.5% of the burn), already
// over half and left at the size `the_floor.ron`'s identical colony runs
// at.
(
    name: "the_bank",
    title: "THE BANK",
    question: "A colony founded at the foot of a raised soil bank, with beetles patrolling its top -- does it dig a gallery into the face rather than a pit in the open?",
    bed: (
        width: 512,
        height: 320,
        soil_depth: 96,
        ground_y: 160,
        compartments: 1,
        founders: 0,
        species: "herb",
        colonies: 0,
        colony_ants: 52,
        colony_species: "ant",
        predators: 0,
        lamp_spacing: 33,
        seed: 1,
        extra_walls: [],
    ),
    settings: [
        (subject: "ant", field: "exposure_cost_per_cell", value: 0.05),
    ],
    placements: [
        Fill(material: "soil", x: 200, y: 144, w: 308, h: 16),
        Colony(species: "ant", x: 170, count: 52),
        Animal(species: "beetle", x: 300),
        Animal(species: "beetle", x: 350),
        Animal(species: "beetle", x: 400),
        Animal(species: "beetle", x: 450),
    ],
    timeline: [
        (at: 3000, every: 6000, until: 0, what: Heap(material: "windfall", x: 150, cells: 20)),
    ],
    horizon: 24000,
)
